// =============================================================================
// Wire Credit Intelligence — REAL sample dataset (European private credit)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Compiled from manager & investor press releases, regulatory/results
// disclosures and trade press. Not affiliated with any data provider; each
// record carries the public source URL(s) it was drawn from.
//
// IMPORTANT — read before relying on any figure:
//  • AUM (managers: aum / aumTotal / aumCredit / groupAum; investors: aum,
//    typicalTicket) is in USD — bn, tickets in m (HOUSE_STYLE R29). Older figures held
//    as €/£-equivalents were RESTATED ONCE at the ECB reference rates in AUM_FX below;
//    `aumFrom` on a record names the restated fields and their original currency.
//    The reported figure in its own currency stays verbatim in `aumText`. Fund sizes
//    (targetSize / raised / hardCap, in m) are stored AS REPORTED — mostly EUR, but not
//    all: `ccy` gives the ISO currency where the fund's own sourced description states
//    the figure (scripts/normalise-data.mjs; absent = not evidenced, never assume EUR).
//  • `estimated: true` / `pcEstimated: true` / "[est]" mark figures that are
//    proxies or not precisely disclosed (very common for LP allocations, where
//    European investors rarely break out "European private credit").
//  • Many fund target sizes / hard caps are undisclosed (null) — left blank
//    rather than guessed. Evergreen funds have no fixed target.
//  • `sources` carry the public URL(s) and `asOf` the reference date.
//  Each record's own `sources` URL(s) + `asOf` date are the authoritative sourcing trail.
// =============================================================================

// When the dataset was last compiled/updated (i.e. the last time data actually changed).
export const DATA_UPDATED = "2026-10-23";

// When the refresh routine last ran (even if it found nothing new) — shown in the
// topbar as "Last refresh" so a run can be confirmed regardless of data changes.
export const LAST_CHECKED = '2026-10-24';
// Time-of-day the routine last ran, as a pre-formatted string WITH a timezone
// label (e.g. "05:22 BST"). Pre-formatted so it renders identically regardless of
// the viewer's browser timezone. Set every run alongside LAST_CHECKED — there are
// four runs a day (~05:00, ~12:00, ~17:00 and ~21:00), so the time tells which run is shown.
export const LAST_CHECKED_TIME = "15:10 BST";

