// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Managers (GPs). `aum` is a US$bn figure for sorting/display (restated once from
// €/£ at AUM_FX below — `aumFrom` records the source currency of each restated
// field); `aumText` states the reported figure in its own currency, as-of and source.
// `aumTotal` (firm-wide) and `aumCredit` (credit platform) are US$bn too, and
// `aum` never exceeds `aumTotal` (spec: tests/aum-currency.mjs).
// `groupAum` (optional, US$bn) is the total group/parent scale, set only where
// `aum` reflects a smaller sleeve/fund figure than the wider group (e.g. Hark's
// parent P10, Eurazeo's group vs. its private-debt sleeve). The Target-focus
// filter gates on group AUM (`groupAum ?? aum`), so a boutique sitting inside a
// large group is correctly excluded from the €1–10bn band.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ECB euro foreign-exchange reference rates used for the one-off USD restatement of
// legacy €/£ AUM figures (2026-10). Source: ECB Data Portal, series EXR.D.USD.EUR.SP00.A
// and EXR.D.GBP.EUR.SP00.A (GBPUSD = USD per EUR ÷ GBP per EUR); AUD, CAD, DKK, CHF, SEK,
// NOK, JPY, SGD, CNY, HKD and PLN from the same day's EXR.D.<ccy>.EUR.SP00.A fixing (added 2026-10-21).
export const AUM_FX = { EURUSD: 1.1188, GBPUSD: 1.3247, AUDUSD: 0.6978, CADUSD: 0.7022, DKKUSD: 0.1497, CHFUSD: 1.2015, SEKUSD: 0.1002, NOKUSD: 0.1049, JPYUSD: 0.006324, SGDUSD: 0.7813, CNYUSD: 0.1494, HKDUSD: 0.1274, PLNUSD: 0.2556, asOf: "2026-10-13", source: "https://data.ecb.europa.eu/data/datasets/EXR" };

